## Required baseline behavior

The new governance record must fail closed when:

1. any exact file hash or byte count drifts;
2. current runtime disposition disagrees with Registry V5;
3. the Downloads candidate is missing or mismatched but is claimed exact;
4. any authority flag is true;
5. target/ideal and current-inventory authority are collapsed;
6. modeled OAV is represented as sensory or hedonic evidence; or
7. a retained downstream artifact is represented as installed runtime code.

The record must preserve the four pre-existing untracked verifier directories
and must not write to registry, formula, inventory, or runtime state.
